# Build-context isolation for deploy/Dockerfile.
#
# The ui-build stage runs `npm ci` from the committed lockfile and rebuilds
# the dist from source, so host-side Node toolchain state, local secrets,
# VCS metadata, and stale build output must never enter the context.
#
# This daemon's BuildKit anchors slash-less patterns to the context root
# only, so every recursive exclusion is written explicitly with the `**/`
# prefix (which matches the root and any depth). Proven by
# test/image/context_sentinel_test.go (real build-context sentinel test).

# VCS metadata, at any depth
**/.git
**/.git/**

# Local secrets — never in a build context, at any depth
**/.env
**/.env.*

# Node toolchain — the image always rebuilds from source; host node state is
# never part of the build
**/node_modules
**/node_modules/**

# Host-side UI build output — the image always rebuilds the dist from source
ui/dist
